WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.513 --> 00:00:04.224
The narrower your perspective,
the fewer advantages you have.

2
00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:06.838
I compared two famous athletes.

3
00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:10.958
One was raised to try many sports,
then chose one.

4
00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:13.100
He kept learning from the others.

5
00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:14.963
Think of an orchestra.

6
00:00:15.727 --> 00:00:17.532
One player knows the violin.

7
00:00:18.302 --> 00:00:22.116
The conductor knows what every
instrument does,

8
00:00:22.761 --> 00:00:24.208
and joins them together.

9
00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:25.752
I swam.

10
00:00:26.656 --> 00:00:27.810
Coaches once said:

11
00:00:28.497 --> 00:00:29.599
swim farther.

12
00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:32.763
Then they learned
it's about the heart rate.

13
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.285
Then that swimming butterfly
makes a freestyler better.

14
00:00:36.895 --> 00:00:39.908
You don't get better at one stroke
without bringing in others.

15
00:00:40.645 --> 00:00:41.977
Write your main stroke.

16
00:00:42.761 --> 00:00:44.813
Write the other strokes
that could build it.

